WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.079 --> 00:00:00.912
(audience applauds)

00:00:00.912 --> 00:00:01.770
- All right it's always
nice to end the hour

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:03.720
with something that brings a little joy.

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:05.610
I feel like this whole
episode has brought some joy,

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:07.099
but whatever, this is what I'm liking.

00:00:07.099 --> 00:00:10.740
(upbeat music) (audience applauds)

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:13.050
Usually when someone
graduates from college,

00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:15.660
there's a lot of family
fanfare and celebration,

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:18.510
but when Texas grad Ashley got her degree,

00:00:18.510 --> 00:00:21.330
there was even more for
the family to celebrate.

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:24.810
Both her mom and dad got
their degrees as well

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:29.063
at the same university on the
same day, which is so cool.

00:00:29.063 --> 00:00:29.899
(audience applauds)

00:00:29.899 --> 00:00:33.660
It marked a first in Texas
Lutheran University's history,

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:36.330
we have all these degree
holders on the line right now

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:38.760
watching on WOAI in Texas.

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.770
Say hi to Ashley and her mama and daddy,

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:42.603
Robin and Greg, everybody.

00:00:42.603 --> 00:00:44.826
(audience applauds)

00:00:44.826 --> 00:00:45.743
- Hi y'all.

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:48.810
- I mean, I guess I'll
start with you, Greg.

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:50.730
Like, first of all, thank
you for your service.

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:52.492
You were in the military,
right, thank you so much.

00:00:52.492 --> 00:00:54.900
(audience applauds)

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:56.850
But is that the reason
you ended up going back

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:58.320
to college 'cause you got outta service

00:00:58.320 --> 00:00:59.790
and you were like, maybe I should finish,

00:00:59.790 --> 00:01:01.500
maybe what I wanted to
do in the first place

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:02.880
is that one of the reasons?

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:05.580
- So I started college
right after high school

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:09.420
and quickly realized that that
wasn't what I wanted to do.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:12.030
I joined the Army, spent 22 years there.

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:15.022
After retiring in 2017,

00:01:15.022 --> 00:01:18.232
I decided I was either going back to work

00:01:18.232 --> 00:01:20.566
or we were going back to school.

00:01:20.566 --> 00:01:23.391
Robin wasn't too excited
about the we part,

00:01:23.391 --> 00:01:26.700
but she came around and
eventually we ended up at

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:28.090
Texas Lutheran University.

00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:29.640
- Oh, that's incredible.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:32.940
So what I mean, Ashley, how
was that going to school

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:33.990
like with your parents

00:01:33.990 --> 00:01:34.860
and graduating with your parents?

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:36.240
That's incredibly cool.

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:37.073
- It was.

00:01:37.073 --> 00:01:38.219
It was really awesome.

00:01:38.219 --> 00:01:42.210
They asked me permission first (all laugh)

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:43.963
so they made sure it was okay.

00:01:43.963 --> 00:01:47.031
And I had been in college
for a year and I had nothing

00:01:47.031 --> 00:01:51.420
but great things to say about
Texas Lutheran University.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:54.720
So I was just so excited to
share that experience with them

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:56.640
and to see them come
to a four year college.

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:58.050
It was just so exciting.

00:01:58.050 --> 00:01:59.160
I was just so proud.

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:02.370
- Yeah, it's such a great
thing for just an inspiration

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:03.810
for a lot of people who wanna go back

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:06.240
and just feel like, well,
maybe I missed the opportunity.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:07.073
You know?

00:02:07.073 --> 00:02:07.906
And you never have.

00:02:07.906 --> 00:02:08.739
You can always go back.

00:02:08.739 --> 00:02:10.980
So what was graduation day like?

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:15.434
- First of all, I was trying
to prepare not to fall,

00:02:15.434 --> 00:02:17.421
while walking the stage.

00:02:17.421 --> 00:02:22.421
And so after that I
was able to turn around

00:02:23.730 --> 00:02:28.730
and it was very surreal
watching my husband

00:02:28.854 --> 00:02:33.854
and daughter, you know,
walk the stage after me.

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:35.093
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:35.093 --> 00:02:36.720
- It was very touching.

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:37.680
- Yeah.

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:39.870
Well, thank you guys so much.

00:02:39.870 --> 00:02:40.928
This is the coolest story.

00:02:40.928 --> 00:02:42.330
(audience applauds)

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:44.250
I don't think I've ever
heard of anything like this

00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:46.410
happening, but Greg and Robin,

00:02:46.410 --> 00:02:48.780
and I'm liking your post right now,

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:50.850
but that's not all our season long partner

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:53.160
pilot pen makers of Frixtion,
the go-to erasable pen

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:54.990
and the Kelly Clarkson
Show want to celebrate

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:57.690
people like you fearlessly
chasing your dreams

00:02:57.690 --> 00:03:00.630
and inspiring everybody in the meanwhile.

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:02.370
So they're gonna give
you a thousand dollars.

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:03.212
How's that sound?

00:03:03.212 --> 00:03:06.212
(audience applauds)

00:03:07.290 --> 00:03:09.360
Congratulations to all of you.

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:10.473
That is so super cool.

00:03:10.473 --> 00:03:12.900
And thank you to all our guests this hour,

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:15.360
Dionne Warwick, Damon Elliot, Mikey Day,

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:17.460
Ivan Marrero, Blake, and Logan.

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:18.957
After the break, if it's
not, try and change it.

00:03:18.957 --> 00:03:19.790
(audience applauds)

